  "description": "This course covers fundamental concepts in data mining including data preprocessing techniques such as data cleaning, transformation, and integration using Python libraries like Pandas and NumPy; exploratory data analysis with visualization tools like Matplotlib and Seaborn; machine learning algorithms such as decision trees, k-means clustering, and association rule mining using Apriori algorithm; data mining methods including classification, regression, clustering, and association rule mining; evaluation metrics like precision, recall, and F-measure; and standards like the CRISP-DM methodology. The course also introduces data mining challenges such as handling missing data, noise, and high dimensionality, and covers advanced techniques like text mining and web mining using technologies like BeautifulSoup and NLP libraries.",
